Our project is SIH1586 Smart Education – Personalized Learning Analytics.

The main problem we address is that teachers may find it difficult to identify every student's learning difficulties early.

To help with this, we developed an interactive dashboard using Python and Streamlit.

Our prototype uses 600 synthetic student records containing learning indicators such as attendance, study hours, quiz scores, and course progress.

We use Pandas for data handling and Scikit-learn for data preprocessing and machine learning.

Our machine-learning algorithm is the Random Forest Classifier, which classifies student records into two categories: needs_support and on_track.

We also developed a rule-based recommendation function to suggest study activities based on student indicators.

The dashboard has six sections: Overview, Student Explorer, Early-Warning Centre, Personalized Study Planner, Dataset Lab, and Model Evaluation.

Our current evaluation report shows approximately 91.33% accuracy on the synthetic test dataset. We understand that this result must be validated using appropriate real-world data before making claims about real student performance.

Our goal is to help teachers understand student learning needs and make more informed decisions about academic support.
